valence_lowq_sph: the SR basis with the Mn TRUE-s WINDOW RESTORED -- for SPHERICAL-d runs ONLY
(doc/SphericalLatticePlan.md I3, 2026-08-13).  Identical to valence_lowq_sr.bsd in every entry except
Mn/O, restored to the EXACT span of the CP2K transcription (IntegrationTests/CP2K/VALENCE-LOWQ-BASIS):
Mn s back to the 7-point window {0.10 .. 24}, Mn d back to 8 (the diffuse 0.18 the SR cell-trim
dropped), O s back to 6 (0.15) and O p back to 5 (0.18).  DISCOVERED 2026-08-13: the CP2K oracles
were ALWAYS in this untrimmed-spherical span -- the SR trims existed for the CARTESIAN cell's
conditioning, and the transcription predates them -- so THIS file under the spherical view is the
first true apples-to-apples basis against the banked CP2K numbers.  THE HISTORY: with CARTESIAN d the 8 d-shell
contaminants (r^2 e^{-ar^2}) span the mid/tight s space, so 7s+8d was rank-deficient (cond 8.2e7,
vet ABORT) and the s window was cut to 2 -- the contaminants then DID the mid-s work.  The SPHERICAL
view (PG_Spherical::MakeSphericalLatticeView) removes the contaminants, which EMPTIES the mid-s
space: measured 2026-08-12, the spherical Mn atom loses 281 mHa (-14.626 -> -14.345 vs the exact
sextet ATOM oracle -14.674) with the trimmed window.  This file restores the physics the trim
delegated to the contaminants.  Under CARTESIAN d this file reproduces the ORIGINAL rank deficiency
-- it is the spherical arm's basis, never the Cartesian arm's.  (CP2K note kept from the parent
file: CP2K solves shell lists in SPHERICAL space, so ITS oracles over the parent file already live
in the trimmed-s spherical span; oracles over THIS file need a fresh CP2K transcription.)

!
